# Native controls (NC)

This is the short form. Before writing code in this area, read the full rules with reasons, bad/good examples and checks: `.ui-polish/rules/01-native-controls.md`.

- **NC-01 Never ship a browser-default `<select>`** (error). Do not render a bare `<select>`. Use the `Select` recipe (Radix listbox) so both the closed trigger and the open list use the project's tokens. A native select is allowed only through the `NativeSelect` recipe (`appearance-none`, token border/radius/height, custom chevron), for long mobile-first lists where the OS picker is the better experience.
- **NC-02 Date and time inputs use the project's picker, not the browser's** (error). Never use `<input type="date">`, `datetime-local`, `month` or `week`. Use the `DatePicker` / `DateRangePicker` recipes (Popover + Calendar). For time, use the `TimePicker` recipe; a native `type="time"` is acceptable only when restyled with tokens.
- **NC-03 File inputs are hidden behind a styled trigger or dropzone** (error). Never show a raw `<input type="file">`. Keep the real input for accessibility but hide it visually (`sr-only`) and drive it from a styled button or dropzone that shows accepted types, size limit, the chosen file names, upload progress and a remove action. Use the `FileUpload` recipe.
- **NC-04 Range sliders are styled** (warning). Use the `Slider` recipe, or style `::-webkit-slider-runnable-track`, `::-webkit-slider-thumb`, `::-moz-range-track` and `::-moz-range-thumb` with tokens. Show the current value next to the slider.
- **NC-05 Colour inputs use a themed picker** (warning). Do not show `<input type="color">`. Use the `ColorPicker` recipe: preset swatches plus a hex field in a Popover. If the full OS picker is needed, keep the native input hidden and open it from a styled swatch button.
- **NC-06 Checkboxes, radios and switches use tokens** (warning). Use the `Checkbox`, `RadioGroup` and `Switch` recipes. At the very least set `accent-color: var(--primary)` globally so native boxes take the brand colour. Checked, indeterminate, focus-visible and disabled states must all be styled.
- **NC-07 No `alert()`, `confirm()` or `prompt()`** (error). Never call the browser dialog functions. Report outcomes with a toast (`Toaster` recipe) or an inline message; ask for confirmation with `ConfirmDialog` / `useConfirm()`; collect a value with a `Dialog` containing a labelled field.
- **NC-08 Tooltips are components, not `title` attributes** (warning). Do not use `title="…"` to explain a control. Use the `Tooltip` recipe, and give icon-only controls an `aria-label`. `title` stays valid on `<iframe>` and `<abbr>`.
- **NC-09 Scrollbars follow the theme** (info). Set `scrollbar-color` and `scrollbar-width` from tokens on the root (plus `::-webkit-scrollbar*` for older WebKit) and set `color-scheme`. For scroll areas inside cards, menus and dialogs use the `ScrollArea` recipe or the same token scrollbar. Never hide scrollbars on content that scrolls.
- **NC-10 Autofill does not repaint inputs** (info). Override `:-webkit-autofill` so autofilled inputs keep the token background and text colour (inset `box-shadow` of the input background plus `-webkit-text-fill-color`). The override is in the tokens recipe.
- **NC-11 Dropdowns and selects: anatomy and behaviour** (error). Every select-like popup must: open on click, Enter, Space and ArrowDown; move with arrow keys, jump with type-ahead, close on Escape and return focus to the trigger; render in a portal above dialogs; flip when it would leave the viewport; cap its height (about 320px) and scroll inside; be at least as wide as its trigger; mark the selected item with a check; show a highlighted state for the keyboard-focused item that is the same as hover.
- **NC-12 Date pickers: anatomy and behaviour** (error). A date picker shows the chosen date in the trigger in the product's date format (never raw ISO), marks today, marks the selection with the primary colour, greys out and blocks dates outside the allowed range, has previous/next month buttons with accessible names, supports arrow-key day navigation, starts the week on the locale's first day, and closes on selection (single date) or on the second click (range). Ranges show the span between the two dates. Offer presets ("Last 7 days") where ranges are common.
- **NC-13 Comboboxes and menus** (warning). Use the `Combobox` recipe when a list has more than about 10 options or is loaded from a server: it filters as the user types, shows a loading row while fetching and a "No results for '…'" row when empty. Menus (`DropdownMenu`) group related items with separators, right-align keyboard shortcuts, put destructive items last in the destructive colour, and align icons in a fixed-width column so labels line up.
